#=GF TP   Cis-reg;
#=GF BM   cmbuild -F CM SEED
#=GF CB   cmcalibrate --mpi CM
#=GF SM   cmsearch --cpu 4 --verbose --nohmmonly -E 1000 -Z 549862.597050 CM SEQDB
#=GF DR   SO; 0000233; mature_transcript;
#=GF DR   GO; 0006382; adenosine to inosine editing;
#=GF RN   [1]
#=GF RM   15361858
#=GF RT   Control of human potassium channel inactivation by editing of a small mRNA
#=GF RT   hairpin.
#=GF RA   Bhalla T, Rosenthal JJ, Holmgren M, Reenan R
#=GF RL   Nat Struct Mol Biol 2004;11:950-956.
#=GF CC   This family represents a group of sequences related to the human potassium
#=GF CC   channel Kv1.1 hairpin element which directs the efficient modification of
#=GF CC   an adenosine to inosine by an adenosine deaminase acting on RNA (ADAR).
#=GF CC   The ADAR modification causes an isoleucine/valine recoding event which
#=GF CC   lies in the ion-conducting pore of the potassium channel. It is thought
#=GF CC   that this editing event targets the process of fast inactivation and
#=GF CC   allows a more rapid recovery from inactivation at negative potentials [1].
#=GF WK   Potassium_channel_RNA_editing_signal
#=GF SQ   85

